## The modules

Every module plugs into female headers on the board, so you can pull them out if one dies. Only the pins that are actually connected are listed. Anything not listed is left empty.

### U_CHG1: Adafruit bq24074 charger (Adafruit 4755)

This is the one with the USB-C port you charge Pocketwick from.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| LIPO | Battery + (VBAT) |
| GND | Ground |
| THERM | Battery temperature sensor (J_BAT1 pin 3) |

Before you plug it in:
- Set its charge jumper to **1.5A**.
- **Cut the THERM jumper**, otherwise the charger ignores the battery's temperature sensor.

### U_BST1: Pololu U3V70F5 5V boost (Pololu 2891)

Turns the battery voltage into 5V for everything.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| VIN | Battery + (VBAT) |
| GND | Ground |
| VOUT | 5V rail (Orange Pi pins 2 and 4, hub, amp, screen, controller) |
| EN | The power switch's VOUT. A 4.7k resistor (R_EN1) pulls it low, so it's off by default |

### U_SW1: Pololu mini pushbutton power switch LV (Pololu 2808)

The on/off latch. It doesn't carry the big battery current, it just turns the boost module on and off through EN.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| VIN | Battery + (VBAT) |
| GND | Ground |
| ON | The power button (when pressed, it gets battery voltage) |
| OFF | Orange Pi pin 12, through a 1k resistor (R_OFF1) |
| CTRL | The 2N3904 transistor (Q_OFF1), for the hold-3-seconds force off |
| VOUT | The boost module's EN pin |

### U_HUB1: Adafruit CH334F 4-port USB hub (Adafruit 5997)

The Orange Pi only has one spare USB port, so this splits it into four.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| VBUS | 5V |
| GND | Ground |
| DP / DM | Upstream: goes to J_OPIUSB1, then the cable to the Orange Pi's USB-C 3.0 port |
| D+1 / D-1 | Port 1: screen touch (J_SCR1) |
| D+2 / D-2 | Port 2: controller (J_CTRL1) |
| D+3 / D-3 | Port 3: sound card socket (J_AUD1) |
| D+4 / D-4 | Port 4: spare, not connected |

### U_FUEL1: Adafruit MAX17048 fuel gauge (Adafruit 5580)

Tells you the battery percentage.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| VIN | 3.3V |
| GND | Ground |
| SCL | I2C clock (Orange Pi pin 5) |
| SDA | I2C data (Orange Pi pin 3) |
| INT | Orange Pi pin 22 (low battery alert) |
| BAT | Battery + (VBAT), so it can measure it |

### U_RTC1: Adafruit DS3231 clock (Adafruit 3013)

Keeps the time when Pocketwick is off. Needs a CR1220 coin cell on the back.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| VIN | 3.3V |
| GND | Ground |
| SCL | I2C clock (Orange Pi pin 5) |
| SDA | I2C data (Orange Pi pin 3) |
| SQW | Orange Pi pin 28 (has a 10k pull-up, R_SQW1) |

### U_HAP1: Adafruit DRV2605L vibration driver (Adafruit 2305)

Drives the vibration motor. The motor's two wires solder straight onto this module.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| VIN | 3.3V |
| GND | Ground |
| SCL | I2C clock (Orange Pi pin 5) |
| SDA | I2C data (Orange Pi pin 3) |
| IN | Orange Pi pin 7 |

### U_AMP1: Adafruit PAM8302 speaker amp (Adafruit 2130)

Makes the speaker loud. The speaker solders to its output terminals.

| Module pin | Connects to |
|---|---|
| VIN | 5V |
| GND | Ground |
| A+ | Audio in: left and right from the sound card mixed together through two 10k resistors (R_ML1, R_MR1) |
| A- | Ground |

