## Connectors on the board

| Ref | What it is | Pin by pin |
|---|---|---|
| J_BAT1 | Battery socket, JST-PH 3-pin | 1 = BAT+ (square pad), 2 = GND, 3 = NTC (temperature sensor) |
| J_SCR1 | Screen, 4-pin header for the micro-USB to Dupont cable | 5V, D-, D+, GND |
| J_CTRL1 | Controller socket, 4-pin header to a USB-C breakout | 5V, D-, D+, GND |
| J_OPIUSB1 | Link to the Orange Pi's USB-C 3.0 port (cable A) | GND, CC (5.1k to ground through R_CC1), D+, D- |
| J_DBG1 | Debug serial, 3.3V only | GND, TX (Orange Pi pin 8), RX (Orange Pi pin 10) |
| J_AUD1 | USB-A socket for the plug-in sound card | 5V, D-, D+, GND (hub port 3) |
| J_JACK1 | 3.5mm jack, sound card plugs in here with a short lead | Tip = left, Ring = right, Sleeve = ground |

**Check J_BAT1 with a multimeter before you plug the battery in.** If the battery's plug is wired the other way round, you'll fry stuff.

For J_DBG1, connect your USB-serial adapter's RX to the board's TX and its TX to the board's RX. They cross over.

