## Buttons

All four are normal 6x6mm tactile buttons.

| Ref | Button | What happens when you press it |
|---|---|---|
| SW_PWR1 | POWER | Connects battery voltage to the power switch's ON pin and to Orange Pi pin 15 (through R_S1/R_S2, so the pin only sees about 3V) |
| SW_PGUP1 | PG UP | Pulls Orange Pi pin 27 to ground (10k pull-up R_PGUP1) |
| SW_PGDN1 | PG DOWN | Pulls Orange Pi pin 29 to ground (10k pull-up R_PGDN1) |
| SW_MENU1 | MENU | Pulls Orange Pi pin 31 to ground (10k pull-up R_MENU1) |

### How the power button works

- **Off, press POWER:** it turns on.
- **On, press POWER once:** Linux shuts down, then pulses pin 12, and the power cuts a few seconds later.
- **Frozen, hold POWER for about 3 seconds:** it force-switches off when you let go. That's the 330k resistor (R_T1) charging the 47uF capacitor (C_T1) until the transistor (Q_OFF1) trips the switch.

